{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-405440-r4525568","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Tuna Fried Rice","sourcePageId":405440,"sourceRevision":"4525568","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-07-21T02:32:26Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Tuna%20Fried%20Rice&oldid=4525568","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T16:18:27.026Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Easy recipes","Category:Inexpensive recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using bean sprout","Category:Recipes using bonito flake","Category:Recipes using cabbage","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using green onion","Category:Recipes using honey","Category:Recipes using rice","Category:Recipes using salt"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"021267ed2c1fece78fe6355d24eedb03c005dfd757495715ebfd3d1f4a430fe7","sourceWikitext":"{{recipesummary|category=Rice recipes|servings=3|time=25 minutes|difficulty=2}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of the United States|American cuisine]] \n\nThis is a simple fried rice made with canned tuna and vegetables, seasoned with honey miso sauce.\n==Ingredients==\n*1 [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] basmati [[Cookbook:Rice|rice]], prepared as a firm and dry pilav\n*[[Cookbook:Olive Oil|Olive oil]]\n*1 medium red [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]], finely [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n*½ cup or more shredded [[Cookbook:Cabbage|cabbage]]\n*1 handful of [[Cookbook:Bean Sprout|bean sprouts]]\n*[[Cookbook:Chili Paste|Red pepper paste]]\n*Hot [[Cookbook:Paprika|paprika]]\n*1 tbsp [[Cookbook:Miso|miso]]\n*½–¾ tbsp [[Cookbook:Honey|honey]]\n*[[Cookbook:Tabasco Sauce|Tabasco]] to taste\n*1 can good-quality [[Cookbook:Tuna|tuna]]\n*2 [[Cookbook:Egg|eggs]]\n*[[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]], if needed\n*Chopped [[Cookbook:Green Onion|scallions]]\n*[[Cookbook:Bonito Flakes|Katsuobushi]]\n\n==Procedure==\n#Prepare a pilaf-style rice. This should be dry with little fat or excess moisture.\n#Sauté the onion in 1 tbsp olive oil.\n#Add the cabbage and bean sprouts.\n#Stir in red pepper paste and paprika.\n#Add the cooked rice.\n#Add the miso and honey, and combine thoroughly.\n#Add Tabasco if desired.\n#Mix in the tuna.\n#Move the rice to one side of the skillet and crack in the eggs.\n#When they are ready, mix the scrambled eggs in with the rice.\n#Garnish with katsuobushi and scallions before serving. \n\n[[Category:Recipes using rice]]\n[[Category:Inexpensive recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bean sprout]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bonito flake]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cabbage]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using salt]]\n[[Category:Recipes using green onion]]\n[[Category:Recipes using honey]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Tuna Fried Rice","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 cup basmati rice, prepared as a firm and dry pilav","sourceText":"1 cup basmati rice, prepared as a firm and dry pilav","amountText":"1 cup basmati rice, prepared as a firm and dry pilav","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"Olive oil","sourceText":"Olive oil","amountText":"Olive oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 medium red onion, finely chopped